    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A person who is enrolled in a clinical study or trial.</skos:definition>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Clinical Study Subject: An individual who is the subject of a clinical study; specifically, a living individual whose physiological and behavioral characteristics and responses are the object of study in a research investigation. [NCIT C70668 (CDISC long form)]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Synonym 'Study participant': clinical context</skos:editorialNote>
