    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">drug</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">product</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">pharmaceutical substance</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">pharmaceutical product</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Qualitative and quantitative composition of a medicinal product in the dose form authorized by the regulatory authority for administration to patients, and as represented with any corresponding regulated product information. NOTE: A medicinal product may contain one or more pharmaceutical products. In many instances, the pharmaceutical product is the manufactured item. However, there are instances where the manufactured item undergoes further preparation before being administered to the patient (as the pharmaceutical product).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA."</dcterms:rights>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-05-23) The session was conducted as a joint evaluation with "compound" and "substance" to clarify conceptual boundaries. Key discussion points: **Label**: Steering Committee recommendation (Cambridge 2025) to use "Pharmaceutical_Product" rather than "Product" was endorsed. **IDMP-O**: Definitions based on ISO standards, not publicly identifiable; confirmed not appropriate for PGO (GitHub issue #54, closed 2025-05). **CDISC/NCIT_C42639**: The CDISC definition (*"Qualitative and quantitative composition of a medicinal product in the dose form authorized..."*) resolvable via NCIT_C42639 and preferred by the expert group. **Should medical devices be included?** The group noted that implanted hips, digital medical devices, and companion diagnostics are not covered by the adopted definition. May warrant a broader core concept in a future PGO phase. **Relevance for R&amp;ED**: The concept must be addressed in early development, not only commercial operations. The group opted for the CDISC definition resolvable via NCIT_C42639. **Outcome:** Consensus on NCIT_C42639/CDISC definition. Recommendation submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pharmaceutical product</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
