  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000009">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms. It may affect the whole body or any of its parts, and its etiology, pathology, and prognosis may be known or unknown.</skos:definition>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D004194"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q12136"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Disease"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://schema.org/MedicalCondition"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://hl7.org/fhir/Condition"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Na619f8c3a78744bea9b0718208c6433e"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Ne24520048da94c34b84e42ade2860a60"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Na92215ccca0d46799ca0824da315cc70"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N24cef505454a426e9e826b6ec3d782f0"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N2ee3d7d99d9e419ea30ab9168d4ab30a"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nb42ebe1a549b43fe91d497c3a9f2d9d8"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N56c3903eccee4dc597a20ea3ce78639c"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N890a2b5e113f4195a2dc7372bcd82290"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N21a45e7d2e154118ae4f738f8afb1547"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">disease</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">medical condition</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">disease</skos:altLabel>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N18af912a063f4856a2fe200bb48d7376"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N901a6a4a9faa402b850ff5b9bd481ada"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ncf42511bd1f14ad6b55aaf1879afbbbf"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N93155fcfbe944faf8b1b0c602a1cd259"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N958ca80c71d84924968a7cbcfdd29824"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N4fe1336a1b54477f8d78793580c9581c"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Nccd5ff41c0d74605a7c04d8cc32ce27a"/>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Disease or Disorder: Any abnormal condition of the body or mind that causes discomfort, dysfunction, or distress to the person affected or those in contact with the person. The term is often used broadly to include injuries, disabilities, syndromes, symptoms, deviant behaviors, and atypical variations of structure and function. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C2991]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Disease: A disease is a disposition (i) to undergo pathological processes that (ii) exists in an organism because of one or more disorders in that organism. [https://disease-ontology.org/?id=DOID:4]</skos:editorialNote>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"Source: National Library of Medicine (NLM). MeSH® is a registered trademark of the U.S. National Library of Medicine."</dcterms:rights>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">Licence of the definition source: NLM Terms — free, attribution required</dcterms:rights>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2024-12-04) The session evaluated three candidate definitions for "disease". The NCIT C2991 definition was initially recommended by multiple steering group members, but the expert group raised several concerns: Too generic — appears to encompass "condition" as well as "disease" The NCIT class hierarchy was considered better than other resources (a relevant advantage for integration) The experts favoured the MeSH D004194 definition for its precision: *"A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms."* Key recommendations: 1. Adopt MeSH D004194 as the definition of "disease". 2. Add a separate core concept "Condition" to PGO, with a distinct definition from "Disease". Subsequent note (April 2025): "disease" and "condition" are not to be considered material entities ("things") or roles, but rather as "processes". This distinction may be relevant for future LinkML modelling. **Outcome:** Consensus on MeSH D004194. Recommendation to add "Condition" as a Phase 2 concept. Submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">disease</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=D004194"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-12</prov:endedAtTime>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q496997"/>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000009</dcterms:identifier>
  </rdf:Description>
