  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000001">
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Na206809d0c4b4fa79edee29599ed9a8d"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N90cc721779584e8e8e09b86fed3b8e0f"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N966bb91c3a404e58ac15b7b4e85f6e1b"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ndc22f1a84bbe45258a530cf4423c175d"/>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Assay: A qualitative or quantitative analysis performed to determine the amount of a particular constituent in a sample or the biological or pharmacological properties of a drug. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C60819]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">BioAssay: A set of instructions, methodology, operations, required reagents, instruments to carry out experiments for the purpose of testing the effect of a perturbing agent in a biological model system, measuring one or multiple effect(s)... [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/bao/classes/http%3A%2F%2Fwww.bioassayontology.org%2Fbao%23BAO_0000015]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Bioassay: A laboratory test or analysis of the biological activity of a substance performed by studying its effect on an organism or in a test tube under controlled conditions. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C16341]</skos:editorialNote>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">assay</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-05-08) The session aimed to reach consensus on the appropriate ontological definition for the concept "Assay" (or "Bioassay") within PGO, and to settle the preferred label. A key conceptual discussion clarified the semantic boundaries between related terms: **Assay** — a planned process measuring a specific activity or property (biological, chemical, physicochemical, sequence-based), typically following a defined protocol. **Experiment** — a broader, less formalized concept that may include multiple assays. **Study** — may encompass multiple experiments or be used synonymously with experiment. **Run** — repeated executions of the same assay or experiment. **Bioassay** — a subset of assays involving biological materials, reagents, or measuring biological properties. **Test** — sometimes used interchangeably with assay in regulatory/pharmacopeial contexts. Four candidate definitions were evaluated: 1. **OBI_0000070** ("A planned process with the objective to produce information about the material entity that is the evaluant, by physically examining it or its proxies.") — considered sufficiently flexible and formally grounded. Ultimately adopted. 2. **NCIT_C16341** (Bioassay) — positively received by multiple experts (Peter McQuilton, Birgit Meldal) for comprehensiveness but links to the PGO concept "Substance", creating potential circular dependency. 3. **BAO_15** — proposed by 2+ partners; criticized as overly complex and including SOP-level information. 4. **NCIT_C60819** — considered too narrow, limited to amount or drug-effect measurement. The group also resolved the label question: **"Assay"** is preferred over "Bioassay" or "Assay/Bioassay" for clarity and generality. "Bioassay" may be considered as a separate concept in future PGO versions. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on OBI_0000070 as the preferred definition with the label "Assay". Formal recommendation submitted to the Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nd1505159469c4785af89d98679eccf2e"/>
