  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000016">
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://hl7.org/fhir/Substance"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C45306"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q214609"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_59999"/>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C45306"/>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">material</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">pharmaceutical substance</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2025-03-06) The session jointly evaluated "Substance" and "Compound". Key findings: **IDMP-O Substance**: The definition appears to be an "information or specification entity" rather than a material entity — a concern flagged for potential IDMP-O engagement (question: what is the rationale for choosing a specification entity over a material entity?). "Substance" has a customary meaning as a functional, contextual term for relatively homogeneous materials (e.g., plastic, wood, tea). **NCIT_C45306** emerged as the consensus candidate: three partners indicated use; endorsed by CS, BM, PMQ. Cross-concept evaluation: "Compound" has more precise chemical composition than "Substance"; "Chemical compound" may be a more accurate label for compound. Some "substances" may also be "compounds" or "drugs" — semantic overlap due to usage. Not all "substances" are "compounds" or "drugs" — there is merit in retaining "substance" as a distinct core concept. Expert group tasked with providing examples of substances that are not compounds or drugs. **Outcome:** Consensus on NCIT_C45306. The group agreed to: (1) evaluate "substance" in conjunction with "compound" — done on 2025-03-06; (2) evaluate in conjunction with "product" — done on 2025-05-23.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA."</dcterms:rights>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Substance: A homogeneous material with a definite composition. [http://hl7.org/fhir/substance.html]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Substance: Specification for matter of defined composition that has discrete existence, whose origin may be biological, mineral or chemical. [https://spec.edmcouncil.org/idmp/ontology/ISO/ISO11238-Substances/Substance]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Chemical Entity: A chemical entity is a physical entity of interest in chemistry including molecular entities, parts thereof, and chemical substances. [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Drug or Chemical by Structure: Substances that are grouped or classified by chemical composition. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C1913]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Substance: Any matter of defined composition that has discrete existence, whose origin may be biological, mineral or chemical. [https://schema.org/Substance]</skos:editorialNote>
