    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Na5de4a67d10a4bda9de1122ecaebcee8"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nf154e1878cf644f4b64b0dfe9080618f"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">indication</skos:prefLabel>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000000"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ned0d5716a4d149a5b6710deb412f91e4"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Ncf54af7aede94ce49ef2d6fd1018c88b"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="N1fa2d172dbcd4ef98e52c8c368e53997"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Nd3aeeff363bc46e8ad17935ad0f9f789"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Nc56b812a2f504f958c5e044d8ee2ee07"/>
    <ns1:preferredSource rdf:nodeID="Na7c55e5c7f664d53ad6a545564e94260"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Disease"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://schema.org/MedicalCondition"/>
    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://hl7.org/fhir/Condition"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sign, signal, circumstance, or symptom which serves to indicate or point out the cause, pathology, treatment, or issue of an attack of disease; the basis for initiation of a treatment for a disease or of a diagnostic test (causal, or symptomatic, or disease-specific indication).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-12</prov:endedAtTime>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <prov:wasAttributedTo>pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py</prov:wasAttributedTo>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Indication: Any abnormal condition of the body ... Includes diseases, injuries, disabilities, disorders, syndromes.</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Indication: The disease or condition the intervention will diagnose, treat, prevent, cure, or mitigate. [https://github.com/cdisc-org/DDF-RA/tree/main/Deliverables/CT]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Indication: Intended use of the Medicinal Product as authorized by the Medicines Regulatory Agency in a jurisdiction</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">indication: Classifier for diseases, symptoms or procedures from medical terminology that is used for, but not limited to, the registration, documentation and safety monitoring of medicinal products. [https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/idmp/ontology/ISO/ISO11615-MedicinalProducts/IndicationAsDiseaseSymptomProcedure]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q496997"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C41184"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">therapeutic indication</skos:altLabel>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000012</dcterms:identifier>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2024-09-11) The session reviewed six candidate definitions for "indication". Several definitions were immediately excluded due to the absence of a resolvable URI. Two candidates remained viable: 1. **NCIT_C41184** — provides a resolvable IRI with CC BY 4.0 license. 2. **CDISC Glossary** — the CDISC definition is preferred by some experts for its clarity ("A health problem or disease that is identified as likely to be benefited by a therapy..."), but CDISC reuses the NCIT code C41184 with its own wording, and no separate URI exists for the CDISC-specific definition. Discussion notes: "Abnormal" or "pathological" are unnecessarily restrictive when defining indication. The distinction between sign and symptom in the NCIT definition was noted. NCIT code C41184 may be acceptable, with all alternate definitions treated as equally valid. The group reached consensus: adopt NCIT_C41184 as the primary definition, with all listed alternate definitions acknowledged as equally valid. **Outcome:** Consensus on NCIT_C41184 as primary definition, CDISC definition as alternative label. Submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C41184"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">indication</rdfs:label>
    <prov:generatedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-24</prov:generatedAtTime>
  </rdf:Description>
