  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGO-00000019">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/PGO/ontology/PGOConceptScheme"/>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">excipient: A constituent of a medicine other than the active substance. [https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/glossary-terms/excipient]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">excipient role: Excipient is a role of a generally pharmacologically inactive substance that is formulated with the active ingredient of a medication. [ChEBI] [http://purl.allotrope.org/ontologies/role#AFRL_0000226]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">excipient: [Pharmacological role of] a generally pharmacologically inactive substance that is formulated with the active ingredient of a medication. [(URL not provided)]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">Synonym 'Formulation ingredient': non-active</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">excipient: Pharmacological role of a generally pharmacologically inactive substance that is formulated with the active ingredient of a medication. [https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/idmp/ontology/ISO/ISO11238-Substances/Excipient]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">excipient: Excipient is defined as a component of a pharmaceutical formulation that serves specific functions, such as aiding in the delivery or stability of the active ingredient. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/pharmacology-toxicology-and-pharmaceutical-science/excipient]</skos:editorialNote>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Pharmaceutical excipient</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Inactive ingredient</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Formulation ingredient</skos:altLabel>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75324"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nae1f2a86ebb5467a9afd2adaa095939b"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="Nac300888b12c4acba0585de71f952013"/>
    <skos:example rdf:nodeID="N21c3761a0cd44ce1bdec14d9fb0289d9"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75324"/>
    <prov:endedAtTime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-03-03</prov:endedAtTime>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">**Round 1** (2026-01-15) The session (2026-01-15) covered Excipient as the first concept (API was the second concept, no consensus reached — see another concept). Multiple candidates were reviewed. The discussion quickly narrowed to two finalists: ChEBI CHEBI_75324 and DRON:00000029. The ChEBI definition ("A generally pharmacologically inactive substance that is formulated with the active ingredient of a medication") was acknowledged as a "negative" definition — it defines excipient by what it is not (not the active ingredient). Despite this limitation, the group converged on it for three reasons: (1) an expert/Roche confirmed ChEBI is the definition adopted by ISO IDMP, giving PGO-IDMP interoperability out of the box; (2) Birgit/Pfizer confirmed the same ("authoritative source &amp; adopted by IDMP-O"); (3) it is concise and from a well-maintained, resolvable source. The DRON definition was positively framed (listing what excipients do: aid manufacture, prolong shelf life, ensure proper administration), which Darko/Novo Nordisk acknowledged is semantically better. However, the phrase "scattered molecular aggregate" was universally criticised as impractical. The IDMP-O and EMA definitions were noted as essentially equivalent to ChEBI or weaker, and did not advance. The EMA definition ("a constituent of a medicine other than the active substance") was considered by some as simpler but without strong reason to prefer it over ChEBI. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on ChEBI CHEBI_75324 as the preferred definition with the label `Excipient`. Formal recommendation submitted to Steering Group.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <dcterms:identifier>PGO-00000019</dcterms:identifier>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">excipient</skos:prefLabel>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <prov:used>2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md</prov:used>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
